# Localhost visual notebook and handwriting editors

## Scope and existing evidence

Provide notebook and handwriting profile tabs in the existing localhost UI,
open/save actions, and a bounded preview with sliders and numeric controls for
every admitted editable scalar.

## Practical acceptance — 2026-11-03

**Basis:** real Firefox against the existing Rust localhost process with
`--profiles-dir`, rather than a mock server or theoretical design.

**Accepted:** one test-owned session edits the nested paper profile (6-mm
grid via slider, 25-mm top margin via numeric input), the notebook profile
(3-mm border radius, date line/placement, page numbers and preprinted flag),
and the separate handwriting statistics profile (exact `ñ` height
override with numeric and slider inputs and full-width seed). It explicitly
saves both native JSON files through authenticated, revision-checked Rust
endpoints. After unsaved changes, both profiles reopen with matching values.

The browser displays an actual Rust PNG notebook page and a separate labeled
seeded *numeric* handwriting preview. All ten admitted handwriting dimensions
have numeric fields and sliders; enum/checkbox controls cover the admitted
page settings. The existing paper editor covers physical dimensions/margins.

**Refused:** a subsequently entered invalid handwriting mean cannot replace
the previously saved native JSON. Existing mock and native Rust tests also
verify stale revisions and unsafe names are rejected. No browser-only save
or silently preserved unsaved model is considered persistent.

**Evidence:** `node --test --test-name-pattern='Firefox edits, saves and
reopens both profiles through Rust localhost'
tests/browser/workspace/adapter-inbound/runtime-frame-ancestors.mjs`, plus
`handwriting-profile.mjs`, `notebook-profile.mjs` and Rust codec/CLI
tests. This finite Linux workflow passed with test-owned profile files.

**Still unavailable:** handwritten glyph outlines, rendered handwritten text,
image overlays and complete notebook content. The PNG is clearly labeled
as a **paper layer**; seeded numbers are not represented as ink. Full glyph
coverage and composed PDF/PNG content remain P4-012/P5-011 work.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical Linux Firefox with authenticated Rust local-file
  controls, numeric/slider round-trip and native preview, 2026-11-03.
- **Delivered:** typed page and handwriting edits, separate file persistence,
  reopened exact values, one accepted and one refused example.
- **Not delivered:** actual handwritten content, full Unicode glyph shapes,
  image overlays or complete final notebook PDF (remaining tasks stay open).
